WEBVTT

00:44:25.329 --> 00:44:31.163
And it really I didn't know that until I
was doing the writing because I found

00:44:31.163 --> 00:44:34.621
the bigger story when I was writing
and buy the bigger story.

00:44:34.663 --> 00:44:38.538
I mean, the story that exceeds the kind
of like, oh, here's you know,

00:44:38.538 --> 00:44:41.829
here's my interesting journey or here's
the big loss I suffered, you know,

00:44:41.829 --> 00:44:47.079
that that I knew that I needed to find a
universal thread that the my journey

00:44:47.079 --> 00:44:51.371
and my loss and my experience would be
had the potential to be expressed in

00:44:51.371 --> 00:44:53.621
a way that other people would
see themselves in it.

00:44:54.121 --> 00:44:57.496
And it took some writing for me to
to figure out how to do that

00:44:57.496 --> 00:44:58.871
or to figure out that that was there.

00:44:59.163 --> 00:45:03.871
You said that being a memoirist is about
learning how to re-enter previous